<p>Also, just in case anyone wants my thoughts (I'm hoping it's abundantly clear what happened, though):</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Author&nbsp;Head-Canon</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The Foundation tried to contain Murphy Law by creating a fictitious 'Pataphysical Department' with 'Thaddeus Thaum', a skilled literary deconstructionist who would deconstruct Murphy's narrative and give him a banal, containable backstory.</p>
<p>It almost worked.</p>
<p>Murphy was able to <em>deconstruct the deconstruction</em>. He started deconstructing the very concept of the article itself &#8212; at which point it all fell apart.</p>
<p>There's also a hidden credits scroll collapsible below the final email. I might make it unhidden later; it's not terribly important, but it kind of hints at how <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-423">Fred</a> managed to escape.</p>
</div>
